+# This also fixes an existing vanilla bug. The lookup used to be `.get(duck_count, 7)` / `.get(duck_count, 0.95)`,
+# and **a missing key falls back to the weakest tier in the whole table**. At 5~8 players (4~6 ducks) every key is missing,
+# so the hunter got the worst gun against the most ducks — exactly backwards.
+# Now the player count is **clamped to the table's key range** before the lookup, so it never lands on the fallback value again.
