+# [MP8] ===== Hip-fire spread (inaccurate without scoping) =====
+#
+# Vanilla fires a perfectly accurate ray from laser_raycast whether scoped or not,
+# so "snap shooting" and "scoped aiming" have the same hit rate, and the scope only lets you see more clearly.
+# This adds a random offset within a cone to **unscoped** shots.
+#
+# Why this makes a good mechanic - the deviation is an **angle**, so the miss distance grows linearly with range.
+# 2° at 125 m is about 4.4 m off (a duck is about 1 m wide → basically unhittable),
+# while within 20 m it's only 0.7 m off (still hittable).
+# That naturally produces "long range needs the scope, close range can hip-fire" without writing any extra rules.
+#
+# zoom_fov_index - 0 = unscoped (FOV 75), 1/2 = scoped. Only 0 gets spread.
+# On 2026-08-15 the user judged 2° too small, so it was raised to 8°.
+#   At 8° the median offset is 125 m→12.4 m, 40 m→4.0 m, 20 m→2.0 m, 10 m→1.0 m
+#   — in other words **you basically can't hit anything unscoped**, with only a slim chance within 10 m.
+#   (A comparison table of the candidate values is in tools\probe\probe18.gd. Run it once after a change to see.)
+@export var mp8_hipfire_spread_deg: float = 8.0
+
+var _mp8_spread_saved_rotation: Vector3 = Vector3.ZERO
+var _mp8_spread_applied: bool = false
